# Generated from: specs/bug-fix-sealed-umbrella-specs-stranded-outside-the-default-branch/requirements.md
# Issue: #157
# Type: Defect regression

@regression @write-spec @upgrade-project @issue-157
Feature: Sealed umbrella specs become canonical before child work
  Sealed umbrella specifications were previously stranded on feature branches,
  while independent child branches trusted worktree presence and history-only
  commit markers. Publication and recovery must now use refreshed default-branch
  content as the canonical contract without broadening mutation scope.

  @regression
  Scenario: Sealing publishes the exact approved spec before child transition
    Given all review gates are approved for an umbrella spec that triggers multi-PR sealing
    When the user approves sealing and transition
    Then the exact approved spec directory is delivered through a spec-only pull request targeting the default branch
    And no version, changelog, manifest, marketplace, or unrelated worktree path is changed
    And child work remains blocked until refreshed remote state proves the merged default branch contains the canonical parent spec

  @regression
  Scenario: Every child entry point fails closed on an uncanonical parent spec
    Given a child issue has a supported body or native relationship to an umbrella issue
    And refreshed default-branch state does not prove a unique canonical parent spec
    When start-issue, write-spec, or write-code would begin child work
    Then the workflow stops before branch, status, spec, plan, delegation, or code mutation
    And the diagnostic identifies the parent and an actionable publication or recovery next step

  @regression
  Scenario: Canonical identity survives squash and rebase history
    Given a spec-only publication is merged without preserving the original seal commit as an ancestor
    And the refreshed default branch contains the exact published spec tree
    When sealing or parent readiness is checked again
    Then the specification is recognized as canonical with its history marker lost
    And no duplicate seal commit or publication pull request is created

  @regression
  Scenario: Upgrade classifies every affected seal state before mutation
    Given initialized disposable projects represent canonical, marker-lost, recoverable-stranded, divergent, ambiguous, and unverifiable seal evidence
    When upgrade-project analyzes their specification and bounded Git state
    Then each relevant exact spec path is assigned the matching seal classification
    And the finding includes the available default branch, tree identity, and source-ref evidence
    And no recovery mutation occurs before explicit approval of an exact finding

  @regression
  Scenario: Upgrade safely prepares one unambiguous stranded spec
    Given the refreshed default branch lacks a spec path
    And all bounded recoverable sources for that path have one full tree identity
    And the user explicitly approves that exact recovery finding
    When upgrade-project revalidates and applies the recovery
    Then only the missing spec directory is restored from the approved full source object ID without staging
    And unrelated dirty files, project-authored content, release artifacts, branches, the index, and GitHub state are unchanged

  @regression
  Scenario: A divergent default-branch spec is never overwritten
    Given the refreshed default branch contains a spec at the canonical path
    And a sealed source ref contains different content at the same path
    When upgrade-project analyzes or applies approved cleanup
    Then the default-branch copy remains canonical and unchanged
    And the differing source is reported as noncanonical with exact evidence
    And no local or remote branch is deleted

  @regression
  Scenario: Publication and recovery are idempotent and preserve existing workflows
    Given disposable repositories cover independent child branches, publication states, history-marker loss, recovery classifications, and already-clean projects
    When the changed contracts and exercises run twice
    Then canonical states proceed and unsafe or ambiguous states fail closed
    And the second seal, publication, or upgrade run creates no additional diff, recovery, or pull request
    And existing single-PR specification, managed-asset upgrade, legacy-layout migration, and explicit human-gate behavior still pass
